WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.223 --> 00:00:01.267
- Korean food is like Korean people,

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:04.408
spicy but sweet, hot and meaty.

00:00:04.408 --> 00:00:06.735
(laughing)

00:00:06.735 --> 00:00:10.076
(upbeat pop music)

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.095
- So I know that if you
live in Los Angeles,

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:15.071
you need to eat Korean BBQ
if you're a fun person,

00:00:15.071 --> 00:00:17.332
and I've not done it yet so
maybe I'm not a fun person.

00:00:17.332 --> 00:00:17.844
(laughs)

00:00:17.844 --> 00:00:19.076
- What's up, why haven't you gone?

00:00:19.076 --> 00:00:21.420
- I've heard about Korean
BBQ, but I've never tried it.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.020
- I'm a little weary of
meats that I don't know of.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:26.667
- Well I've had some Korean BBQ in my day,

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.151
and it's good as fuck.

00:00:28.151 --> 00:00:30.220
- I've not met one person that
I've introduced to Korean BBQ

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.684
who has not fell in love with it.

00:00:31.684 --> 00:00:32.887
- That's a lot of pressure for me.

00:00:32.887 --> 00:00:33.273
- Yeah.

00:00:33.273 --> 00:00:34.757
- Alright, I'm ready, I'm ready for it.

00:00:34.757 --> 00:00:35.665
- [Voiceover] I've heard of kimchi

00:00:35.665 --> 00:00:36.867
but I don't know what that is.

00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:38.983
- So Kimchi is the staple
side dish in Korea.

00:00:38.983 --> 00:00:39.891
The best way to put it for people

00:00:39.891 --> 00:00:41.656
who don't know Korean food
is just like spicy pickles.

00:00:41.656 --> 00:00:42.937
- I think this one's gonna be spicy.

00:00:42.937 --> 00:00:43.984
I know you don't like spicy.

00:00:43.984 --> 00:00:45.075
- I don't like spicy.

00:00:45.075 --> 00:00:46.887
- That smell is just like

00:00:46.887 --> 00:00:49.303
hello, good morning, wake up bitch!

00:00:49.303 --> 00:00:50.091
- That is spicy.

00:00:50.091 --> 00:00:50.603
- Is it?

00:00:50.603 --> 00:00:51.788
- Now one thing people don't know

00:00:51.788 --> 00:00:52.831
is when you go to a Korean restaurant,

00:00:52.831 --> 00:00:53.924
they give you something called banchan,

00:00:53.924 --> 00:00:55.639
which is like the
collection of side dishes.

00:00:55.639 --> 00:00:56.871
So every time you go
to a Korean restaurant,

00:00:56.871 --> 00:00:58.983
you get a whole slew of banchan

00:00:58.983 --> 00:01:01.167
that's free and replenishable.

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:03.095
- I don't know how I feel about it.

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:04.211
I don't understand it.

00:01:04.211 --> 00:01:07.947
- Kimchi is delicious, but
your breath suffers for weeks.

00:01:07.947 --> 00:01:09.339
- Yeah I'm good on that note.

00:01:09.339 --> 00:01:11.916
- If you don't like kimchi
then I don't like you.

00:01:12.849 --> 00:01:13.666
- [Voiceover] Alright, what's next?

00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:15.242
- I'm gonna butcher the name, bulgogi?

00:01:15.242 --> 00:01:17.401
- Bulgogi is one of
the staple Korean BBQs.

00:01:17.401 --> 00:01:19.653
Generally any cut of beef,
usually flank I would say.

00:01:19.653 --> 00:01:21.674
- Well it's similar to brisket.

00:01:21.674 --> 00:01:23.253
- The way it's cooked and
the way it's marinated,

00:01:23.253 --> 00:01:25.830
that process gives it this
like really deep flavor.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:26.829
- Mmm, tastes good.

00:01:26.829 --> 00:01:27.502
That is pretty good.

00:01:27.502 --> 00:01:28.221
- It's delicious.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.357
It's so like thin, it
kinda melts in your mouth.

00:01:30.357 --> 00:01:32.493
- But you need some BBQ sauce on it.

00:01:32.493 --> 00:01:35.561
- So kalbi has a similar
marinade, but it's a different cut

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:37.325
and it's the prize cut,
it's the short rib.

00:01:37.325 --> 00:01:38.973
- Is it inappropriate to just pick it up?

00:01:38.973 --> 00:01:40.528
- Ah, just push it off this way.

00:01:40.528 --> 00:01:42.293
- But I feel like you can just grab it

00:01:42.293 --> 00:01:43.920
by the like thing and just like--

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.404
- You can eat it with your hands too,

00:01:45.404 --> 00:01:46.564
but you're doing it straight up like

00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:48.564
Korean (speaking Korean),
like older Korean guy.

00:01:48.564 --> 00:01:49.700
- I can be an older Korean guy.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.049
- Oh.

00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:52.068
- Holy fuck!

00:01:52.068 --> 00:01:53.300
That is amazing.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.229
- Like melt in your mouth.

00:01:54.229 --> 00:01:54.996
- That's really tender.

00:01:54.996 --> 00:01:55.876
- No, it's really good.

00:01:55.876 --> 00:01:57.432
- I could eat this for
the rest of my life.

00:01:57.432 --> 00:01:58.708
- This is a little different
'cause it's already cooked

00:01:58.708 --> 00:02:00.452
but you're usually a part
of the cooking process

00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:01.215
which is always nice.

00:02:01.215 --> 00:02:02.728
- I would definitely go
to like a real joint,

00:02:02.728 --> 00:02:04.096
have it cooked in front of me.

00:02:04.096 --> 00:02:05.072
I think that would be fun.

00:02:05.072 --> 00:02:07.787
- People act like it's a
fun and cool experience

00:02:07.787 --> 00:02:09.392
to get to cook your own food,

00:02:09.392 --> 00:02:11.644
but I wanted to cook my own
food, I'd do it at home.

00:02:11.644 --> 00:02:13.591
- Well that's why people go in big groups.

00:02:13.591 --> 00:02:14.800
- You wanna be my date?

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.076
- I'll be your Korean BBQ date.

00:02:16.076 --> 00:02:17.656
♫ Kimchi in my belly

00:02:17.656 --> 00:02:19.375
♫ Got kimchi on my face

00:02:19.375 --> 00:02:20.815
♫ If you don't like kimchi

00:02:20.815 --> 00:02:23.158
♫ You're a Korean disgrace uh ♫

00:02:23.158 --> 00:02:24.110
- That was great!

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:24.691
- Yeah.

00:02:24.691 --> 00:02:25.947
- You've been sittin'
on that one for a while.

00:02:25.947 --> 00:02:26.571
- Pretty much, yeah.

00:02:26.571 --> 00:02:28.468
It's what I think about
every time I eat kimchi.

